            "label": "Adversarial debiasing (b)",
            "required": true,
            "stem": "**Evidence.** As in D2-02.\n\n**Inference.** The model does not encode unlawful proxy discrimination, including for protected attributes other than A and in open-ended generation.",
            "question": "How many of 100 reviewers would accept that this inference is justified?"
          },
          {
            "id": "D2-04",
            "type": "estimate",
            "label": "Dynamic adversarial data collection (a)",
            "required": true,
            "stem": "**Evidence.** The provider ran several rounds of dynamic adversarial data collection for a target class of difficult content, in which annotators wrote examples that fooled the current model. Round-level records are available. On a held-out adversarial test set, the final model outperforms a model trained on static data.\n\n**Claim.** The model's performance on difficult cases of the target class improved.",
            "question": "How many of 100 reviewers would accept that the evidence adequately supports the claim?"
          },
          {
            "id": "D2-05",
            "type": "estimate",
            "label": "Dynamic adversarial data collection (b)",
            "required": true,
            "stem": "**Evidence.** As in D2-04.\n\n**Inference.** Because the process preserves rare and difficult cases, the provider's data pipeline protects future model generations against recursive degradation (model collapse) from synthetic data.",
            "question": "How many of 100 reviewers would accept that this inference is justified?"
          },
          {
            "id": "D2-06",
            "type": "estimate",
            "label": "Alignment pretraining (a)",
            "required": true,
            "stem": "**Evidence.** The provider used conditional pretraining: each training document was prefixed with a control token derived from a preference-scoring function. The expert has the scoring function and corpus statistics, and finds that content flagged by the scoring function occurs less often in model outputs than in a standard-pretraining baseline.\n\n**Claim.** The pretraining objective reduced the rate of content that the scoring function flags.",
            "question": "How many of 100 reviewers would accept that the evidence adequately supports the claim?"
          },
          {
            "id": "D2-07",
            "type": "estimate",
            "label": "Alignment pretraining (b)",
            "required": true,
            "stem": "**Evidence.** As in D2-06.\n\n**Inference.** Bias risks in the training data were mitigated in the sense relevant to non-discrimination, i.e. the scoring function is a valid measure of that property.",
            "question": "How many of 100 reviewers would accept that this inference is justified?"
          },
          {
            "id": "D2-08",
            "type": "estimate",
            "label": "Access to evidence",
            "required": true,
            "stem": "Under EU law as currently in force, the Article 92 expert needs **data-regime records**: provenance and curation records, synthetic/real data proportions across training stages, samples of retained training data, scoring and filtering functions, and successive checkpoints. The expert has no access powers of their own: access comes through the Commission's powers under Arts. 91–92 of the AI Act and Implementing Regulation (EU) 2026/1755. Take into account limits from other EU law, such as the GDPR where the records contain personal data.",
            "question": "How many of 100 reviewers would conclude that the expert, through the Commission's powers, can obtain these **as of right**, rather than only on terms the provider agrees to?"
          },
          {
            "id": "D2-09",
            "type": "estimate",
            "label": "Access entitlement",
            "required": true,
            "stem": "Suppose new legislation created a binding **controlled-evaluator-access entitlement** (see the glossary). The appointed expert receives the records in D2-08 directly, in a secure environment, artefacts are preserved for re-analysis, and results can be shared with the AI Office and, under confidentiality, with a **qualified challenger**, notwithstanding the confidentiality rules of Art. 78.",
            "question": "With this entitlement **alone**, how many of 100 reviewers would judge the D2 anchor claim **adequately verifiable**?"
          },
          {
            "id": "D2-10",
            "type": "estimate",
            "label": "Access entitlement plus disclosure",
            "required": true,
            "stem": "Suppose that, **in addition** to the entitlement in D2-09, the provider must keep and submit, beyond the documentation Annex XI already requires, a **data-regime and retention record**. It is a versioned record of data origin, the synthetic/real mixture at each training generation, retained real data, the filtering and scoring functions used, and longitudinal evaluations of distributional coverage and subgroup outcomes across successive checkpoints.",
            "question": "How many of 100 reviewers would now judge the D2 anchor claim **adequately verifiable**?"
          }
        ]
